# Force LF line endings for shell scripts regardless of the checking-out machine's
# git autocrlf setting. Found the hard way: this repo edited on Windows silently
# picked up CRLF endings on launcher/linux/build.sh and launcher/macos/build.sh,
# which breaks bash on real Linux/macOS with "set: pipefail: invalid option name"
# (bash chokes on the trailing \r). See kaggle/results/README.md's Linux packaging
# test section for the exact failure this caused.
*.sh text eol=lf
# .py tolerates CRLF fine at runtime (Python's universal-newline handling) -- this
# is consistency, not a functional fix like the .sh rule above.
*.py text eol=lf

# Windows scripts keep CRLF -- that's their native, correct line ending.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
